---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How VideoVault handles media, backups, purchases, and support messages."
	canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
	<article class="legal container">
		<nav class="legal__nav" aria-label="Legal">
			<a href="/">Home</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.privacy} aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.terms}>Terms of Use</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.support}>Support</a>
		</nav>

		<h1>VideoVault Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="legal__meta">
			<strong>Effective date:</strong> July 16, 2026<br />
			<strong>Last updated:</strong> October 12, 2026
		</p>

		<blockquote>
			VideoVault is designed to process your media locally. VideoVault does not operate a developer
			server that receives or stores your videos, audio files, recordings, Private Lists, or backup
			contents.
		</blockquote>

		<h2>1. Scope</h2>
		<p>
			This Privacy Policy explains how VideoVault (“VideoVault,” “the app,” “we,” or “us”)
			handles information when you use the app, contact support, or purchase a Pro plan.
		</p>

		<h2>2. Media and app data stored on your device</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault stores imported media, generated media, recordings, Private Lists, thumbnails,
			preferences, and related metadata inside the app’s local storage on your device.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				VideoVault accesses photos or files only when you choose to import, save, export, share, back
				up, or restore content.
			</li>
			<li>
				Microphone access is used only when you choose to record audio or create a voiceover.
			</li>
			<li>Your media is not automatically uploaded to us.</li>
			<li>VideoVault does not sell your media or app data.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>3. Backup and restore</h2>
		<p>
			When you use Full Library Backup, VideoVault creates a backup locally on your device. You
			choose where to save it, such as iCloud Drive, On My iPhone/iPad, an external drive, or another
			file provider.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Backup files can contain videos, audio files, recordings, Private Lists, and media metadata.
			</li>
			<li>VideoVault does not upload backup contents to a developer-operated server.</li>
			<li>
				You are responsible for storing backup files in a trusted location and protecting access to
				them.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>4. App deletion and device changes</h2>
		<p>
			Deleting VideoVault removes the app’s locally stored media and Private Lists from that device.
			Before deleting the app or changing devices, export a Full Library Backup to an external
			location. Off-device originals that remain in Photos, Files, or another storage service are not
			deleted by VideoVault.
		</p>

		<h2>5. Purchases</h2>
		<p>
			Monthly and Yearly Pro subscriptions and the Lifetime Pro non-consumable purchase are processed
			by Apple through the App Store and StoreKit. VideoVault receives transaction and entitlement
			status needed to unlock or restore Pro features. We do not receive your full payment card details.
		</p>

		<h2>6. Feedback and support email</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault does not automatically collect your email address. If you choose to email support,
			your email address and the information you include are transmitted through your email provider
			and received at{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>. The address is routed to our
			support inbox through Cloudflare Email Routing.
		</p>
		<p>
			Support messages are used to answer your request, investigate bugs, improve the app, and
			maintain reasonable support records. Do not include private media unless you intentionally
			choose to share it. You may request deletion of a support message by contacting us.
		</p>

		<h2>7. Analytics, advertising, and tracking</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault 1.0 does not include third-party advertising, cross-app tracking, or a
			developer-operated analytics service. Apple may provide developers with aggregated App Store,
			purchase, and diagnostic information under Apple’s own terms and privacy practices.
		</p>

		<h2>8. Permissions</h2>
		<p>
			Depending on the feature you use, VideoVault may request access to Photos, Files, the
			microphone, and media playback capabilities. You can manage permissions in iOS or iPadOS
			Settings. Denying a permission may prevent the related feature from working but does not
			prevent unrelated features from operating.
		</p>

		<h2>9. Data retention and deletion</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Local app data remains until you delete it in VideoVault, replace the library during restore,
				or delete the app.
			</li>
			<li>Backup files remain in the location you selected until you delete them.</li>
			<li>
				Support emails are kept only as reasonably needed for support, security, and legal
				recordkeeping.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>10. Children</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault is a general-purpose media utility and is not directed specifically to children. We
			do not knowingly collect personal information from children through a developer-operated
			account or server.
		</p>

		<h2>11. Security</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault uses Apple platform protections and app sandboxing. No storage or transmission method
			is completely secure, so protect your device, Apple Account, email account, and backup locations
			with appropriate security controls.
		</p>

		<h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this policy when VideoVault’s features or legal requirements change. The updated
			date will appear at the top of this page. Material changes will be reflected in the app or its
			App Store information when appropriate.
		</p>

		<h2>13. Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Privacy and support questions:{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>
